# Vercel Configuration - Ready to Deploy

This file enables automatic deployment to Vercel.

[Learn more about Vercel deployment](https://vercel.com/docs)

## One-Click Deployment

Click the button below to deploy to Vercel:

[![Deploy to Vercel](https://vercel.com/button)](https://vercel.com/new/clone?repository-url=https://github.com/Dikshathorve/Resumind-new&env=VITE_API_URL&envDescription=Your%20backend%20API%20URL&project-name=resumind&framework=vite&rootDirectory=frontend)

## Manual Deployment Steps

1. Push code to GitHub (Already done ✓)
2. Go to [Vercel Dashboard](https://vercel.com/dashboard)
3. Click "New Project"
4. Import GitHub Repository: `Dikshathorve/Resumind-new`
5. Configure:
   - Framework: React
   - Root Directory: `frontend`
   - Build Command: `npm run build`
   - Output Directory: `dist`
6. Add Environment Variable:
   - Key: `VITE_API_URL`
   - Value: Your backend API URL (e.g., `https://your-backend.azurewebsites.net/api`)
7. Click "Deploy"

## After Deployment

Your frontend will be live at your unique Vercel URL. You can:
- Add a custom domain
- Configure CI/CD triggers
- View analytics and logs
- Set up automatic deployments on push

